  "description": "Intracranial EEG (ECoG grids/strips and depth electrodes) recorded from 17 adults undergoing inpatient seizure-localization monitoring. Recordings were made before, during and after continuous 100 Hz direct electrical stimulation of the lateral orbitofrontal cortex and other sites, as well as during single-pulse electrical stimulation. The data accompany a study of the effect of orbitofrontal stimulation on mood in individuals with symptoms of depression, and are converted to iEEG-BIDS.",
  "methods_description": "Recordings were acquired with Natus clinical, Tucker-Davis Technologies, or NeuroOmega systems during continuous 100 Hz stimulation (task-stim) and single-pulse stimulation (task-sps). Stimulation amplitude and site were derived from file names. Data were converted from MATLAB v7.3 to BrainVision float32 format without filtering, resampling, or re-referencing.",
